{#- Project site template. Rendered by demo/build_site.py into docs/index.html.
    Never type a number here: pass it in from build_site and format it with a
    filter (f3, f2, signed, pval, pct, n, num, pow10, label). The build fails
    if a number in the page text, including <template> content, has no source. -#}
{% set T = r.test %}
{% set V = r.val %}
{% macro cite(key) %}<a class="cite" href="#ref-{{ ref_no[key] }}" data-ref="{{ ref_no[key] }}" aria-label="Reference {{ ref_no[key] }}">[{{ ref_no[key]|label }}]</a>{% endmacro %}
{% macro dci(v) %}{{ v.mean|signed }} [{{ v.lo|f3 }}, {{ v.hi|f3 }}]{% endmacro %}
{% macro sd(a) %}{{ a.mean|f3 }} ± {{ a.std|f3 }}{% endmacro %}
{% macro sw(k) %}<span class="sw" style="background:var(--c-{{ k }})"></span>{% endmacro %}
{% macro bold(col, k) %}{% if best[col] == k %} class="best"{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
{% macro slides(n) %}{{ n|n }} slide{% if n != 1 %}s{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Kidney Vessel Segmentation</title>
  <meta name="description" content="A controlled ablation of stain augmentation and stain normalisation for U-Net segmentation of PAS-stained human kidney.">
  <meta name="color-scheme" content="dark">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Source+Serif+4:ital,opsz,wght@0,8..60,400;0,8..60,600;1,8..60,400&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
</head>
<body>
<div class="page">
<article>
  <header class="col">
    <p class="kicker">Project · Computational pathology</p>
    <h1>Stain-robust blood-vessel segmentation in kidney histology</h1>
    <p class="dek">A controlled ablation of stain augmentation and stain normalisation for U-Net segmentation of PAS-stained human kidney, built as a reproducible PyTorch pipeline with a statistics layer and an interactive demo.</p>
    <p class="meta"><a href="{{ urls.repo }}">Source</a><a href="{{ urls.lab }}">Interactive demo</a><a href="{{ urls.weights }}">Weights</a><span>Yaser Alharbi · {{ year|num }}</span></p>
    <p class="stack">PyTorch · segmentation-models-pytorch · Albumentations · NumPy · SciPy · Streamlit</p>
  </header>

  <section class="col">
    <h2><span class="n">{{ sec.overview|label }}</span>Overview</h2>
    <p>Stain variation between slides and laboratories is a dominant source of domain shift in histopathology. This project isolates one variable, the treatment of stain colour, and measures its effect on cross-slide vessel segmentation using the HuBMAP <i>Hacking the Human Vasculature</i> dataset {{ cite("hubmap") }}. Four otherwise identical training regimes are compared: an RGB-augmentation baseline, HED stain augmentation {{ cite("ruifrok") }}, Macenko normalisation {{ cite("macenko") }}, and both combined, as studied on H&amp;E by Tellez et al. {{ cite("tellez") }}.</p>
    <p>HED augmentation improved test Dice by <span class="num">{{ T.vs.hed.mean|signed }}</span> ({{ ci_level|pct(0) }} CI <span class="num">[{{ T.vs.hed.lo|f3 }}, {{ T.vs.hed.hi|f3 }}]</span>, Holm-adjusted <span class="num"><i>p</i> = {{ T.vs.hed.p_holm|pval }}</span>). With a PAS-fitted reference, Macenko normalisation had no detectable effect on test Dice (<span class="num">{{ T.vs.mac.mean|signed }}</span>, CI <span class="num">[{{ T.vs.mac.lo|f3 }}, {{ T.vs.mac.hi|f3 }}]</span>), and the combined arm, trained on normalised inputs, gave a small gain that did not survive correction (<span class="num">{{ T.vs.full.mean|signed }}</span>, <span class="num"><i>p</i> = {{ T.vs.full.p_holm|pval }}</span>). On the expert-labelled validation slide, all three stain-aware arms improved on the baseline.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="col">
    <h2><span class="n">{{ sec.pipeline|label }}</span>Pipeline</h2>
    <p>The system is config-driven: a single YAML file resolves into a frozen <code>Config</code>, and every stage reads from it. Each stage is idempotent and writes to disk, so the sweep can be interrupted and resumed without retraining completed runs.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="wide pipe-wrap">
    <figure class="pipe-fig">
      <svg class="pipeline" viewBox="0 0 440 486" role="img" aria-label="Pipeline: kidney tiles and vessel annotations are split by slide, fan out into four colour-transform arms, then a U-Net is trained and evaluated per seed and results land in one summary file.">
<defs><marker id="arr" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" fill="currentColor"/></marker></defs>
<path class="edge" d="M220.0,70 V116" fill="none" marker-end="url(#arr)"/>
